{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Wandering</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and חמורו תועה, and אדם תועה מדרך השכל. To teach you that he wandered and went off the road and entered the fields to search. Or: his ass was wandering, and we say all the more so the loss of his own body — if one sees his fellow wandering on the road, he must return him, and his brothers did not attend to the loss of his body; therefore they wandered from the path of reason." "<b>And the man asked him</b> in gematria: the angel Gabriel asked him."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:51.699047106Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}